Practice Problems — Topic 8
Q1. DRC error interpretation:
A student runs DRC on their flyback PCB and gets these errors. For each, explain what went wrong and how to fix it:
(a) "Track on F.Cu at (23.4, 15.2) too close to pad on B.Cu at (23.4, 14.9) — clearance 0.08mm, minimum 0.2mm"
(b) "No connection between pad 3 of C1 and pad 1 of C2 (PGND net)"
(c) "Via drill size 0.2mm smaller than minimum 0.3mm at (45.0, 30.0)"
(d) "Courtyard overlap between U1 and C5"
(e) "Clearance between net PGND and net SGND: 3.2mm, required 6.4mm at (57.0, 40.0)"
Q2. Gerber file verification checklist:
You upload your flyback Gerber files to a free online viewer. Describe what you should verify in each file:
(a) Top copper layer (F.Cu)
(b) Bottom copper layer (B.Cu) — specifically what does the primary-secondary gap look like?
(c) Top silkscreen (F.Silkscreen)
(d) Top soldermask (F.Mask) — what should you look for around the MOSFET DPAK pad?
(e) Drill file — how many holes should appear and what sizes?
Q3. Manufacturing specification verification:
Before submitting your flyback PCB to JLCPCB, verify these parameters match your design:
(a) Your narrowest trace is 0.3mm. JLCPCB standard process minimum is 0.127mm (5mil). Is your design within capability?
(b) Your smallest via drill is 0.3mm. JLCPCB minimum is 0.2mm. Is your design within capability?
(c) You specified 2oz copper. JLCPCB standard is 1oz — you must select 2oz from the dropdown (additional cost). What is the approximate cost difference for 5 boards?
(d) The board has a primary-to-secondary slot (a physical gap cut through the board). This requires a special routing operation. How do you add a board slot in KiCad and does JLCPCB support internal slots?
(e) Your MOSFET DPAK thermal pad requires exposed copper (no soldermask) on the pad. Verify this in the soldermask Gerber — what should the DPAK footprint look like in the soldermask layer?
Q4. BOM procurement planning:
Using your flyback capstone BOM from this topic:
(a) Which components are available at Ikeja Computer Village? Which may need to be ordered online?
(b) The STD5NK60Z MOSFET may not be stocked locally. Name two alternative 650V N-channel MOSFETs with similar or better specifications that might be available from Mouser or AliExpress.
(c) The MBRS4200 Schottky diode (200V, 4A): if not available locally, name an alternative with equivalent or better specs.
(d) Calculate total component cost estimate in Nigerian Naira for all components (research approximate prices from Ikeja or online suppliers).
(e) The transformer T1 must be wound manually. List all materials needed to wind it (core, bobbin, wire gauges and lengths for each winding, tape for insulation layers) and estimate cost.
